<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title="AgentLair vs. Lyrie, ARIA, Experian + AWS, Visa — May 2026"
      description="How AgentLair compares to Lyrie ATP, ARIA, Experian, AWS AgentCore, Visa TAP, MCP, ERC-8004 — agent identity, credentials, and behavioral trust."
    />
    <meta property="article:modified_time" content="2026-05-14T00:00:00Z" />
    <script type="application/ld+json">{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "AgentLair vs. The Field — May 2026 Identity-Protocol Comparison",
  "description": "How AgentLair compares to Lyrie ATP, ARIA, Experian, AWS AgentCore, Visa TAP, MCP, ERC-8004 — agent identity, credentials, and behavioral trust.",
  "datePublished": "2026-05-01",
  "dateModified": "2026-05-14",
  "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "AgentLair", "url": "https://agentlair.dev" },
  "mainEntityOfPage": "https://agentlair.dev/compare",
  "mentions": [
    { "@type": "SoftwareApplication", "name": "Lyrie Agent Trust Protocol", "url": "https://github.com/OTT-Cybersecurity-LLC/lyrie-ai" },
    { "@type": "SoftwareApplication", "name": "ARIA Protocol", "url": "https://aria.bar" },
    { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Experian Agent Trust", "url": "https://www.experianplc.com" }
  ]
}</script>
    <script type="application/ld+json">{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does AgentLair compare to Lyrie ATP?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Lyrie ATP is an open identity standard for agent credentials. AgentLair is a behavioral-trust runtime for the same agents after they're credentialed. The two are complementary: an ATP-credentialed agent operating across organizations is the natural input to AgentLair's behavioral attestation."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is Experian Agent Trust a replacement for AgentLair?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. Experian's Agent Trust binds a verified human to an authorized agent and scores fraud risk at transaction time. It does not monitor agent behavior across organizations during execution. AgentLair closes that runtime gap."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does AgentLair do that Lyrie, ARIA, and Experian don't?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Cross-organizational behavioral attestation — a portable, observed record of how an agent has acted across every organization that has issued it work."
      }
    }
  ]
}</script>
